# DECSET 9001 is Windows win32-input-mode. The terminal tracks it so that key
# encoding can defer to the Windows-native input contract while it is on, and
# DECRQM reports it as a recognised, set mode rather than unknown.
size: 12x3
description: win32-input-mode is tracked and reported by DECRQM

--- input
\e[?9001h\e[?9001$p

--- expect-reply
\e[?9001;1$y
